{
  "id": "al9",
  "title": "Loops",
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "al9-l1",
      "title": "Counting Down",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "The classic 8080 loop: put the count into a register, do the work, DCR the register, and JNZ back while it isn't zero.",
        "DCR sets the zero flag when the count reaches 0, so JNZ falls through and the loop ends.",
        "The loop body runs exactly as many times as the starting count."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "006   ; 000: MVI B",
          "005   ;      5",
          "076   ; 002: MVI A",
          "000   ;      0",
          "306   ; 004: ADI   ← loop",
          "003   ;      3",
          "005   ; 006: DCR B",
          "302   ; 007: JNZ loop",
          "004   ;      address 004 (low byte)",
          "000   ;      (high byte)",
          "323   ; 012: OUT 377",
          "377   ;      port 377",
          "166   ; 014: HLT"
        ],
        "output": [
          "LEDS ○○○○●●●● = 15"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "al9-l1-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "Which two instructions end a counting loop?",
          "options": [
            "DCR and JNZ",
            "INR and JMP",
            "CPI and JC",
            "MOV and HLT"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Count down, jump back while not zero."
        },
        {
          "id": "al9-l1-e2",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "How many times does the loop body run if B starts at 5?",
          "options": [
            "5",
            "4",
            "6",
            "Forever"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "5, 4, 3, 2, 1, then 0 ends it."
        },
        {
          "id": "al9-l1-e3",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What do the lights show?",
          "code": [
            "006   ; 000: MVI B",
            "004   ;      4",
            "076   ; 002: MVI A",
            "000   ;      0",
            "306   ; 004: ADI   ← loop",
            "003   ;      3",
            "005   ; 006: DCR B",
            "302   ; 007: JNZ loop",
            "004   ;      address 004 (low byte)",
            "000   ;      (high byte)",
            "323   ; 012: OUT 377",
            "377   ;      port 377",
            "166   ; 014: HLT"
          ],
          "options": [
            "12",
            "4",
            "3",
            "16"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "4 rounds, adding 3 each time."
        },
        {
          "id": "al9-l1-e4",
          "type": "find_bug",
          "prompt": "This loop should run 3 times, but it runs 253 times. Which line is wrong?",
          "code": [
            "006   ; 000: MVI B",
            "003   ;      3",
            "074   ; 002: INR A   ← loop",
            "004   ; 003: INR B",
            "302   ; 004: JNZ loop",
            "002   ;      address 002",
            "000   ;      (high byte)",
            "166   ; 007: HLT"
          ],
          "answer": 3,
          "explanation": "INR B counts up from 3 and only reaches 0 after wrapping around past 255. It should be DCR B (005)."
        },
        {
          "id": "al9-l1-e5",
          "type": "fill_blank",
          "prompt": "Count down register C.",
          "code": [
            "___   ; DCR C"
          ],
          "options": [
            "015",
            "014",
            "025",
            "005"
          ],
          "answer": "015",
          "explanation": "DCR C = 0 1 5."
        },
        {
          "id": "al9-l1-e6",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "Why does the loop work with DCR but not with MOV?",
          "options": [
            "DCR sets the zero flag, MOV doesn't",
            "MOV is slower",
            "MOV can't use B",
            "It works with both"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "JNZ needs a flag that was set by arithmetic."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "al9-l2",
      "title": "Loops over Memory",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "Combine a counting loop with HL: LXI H points to a table, and every round does INX H to move on.",
        "That's how the Altair added up a list of numbers, searched a table, or copied a block of memory.",
        "One register counts the rounds, HL walks through memory, A collects the result."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "041   ; 000: LXI H table",
          "020   ;      address 020 (low byte)",
          "000   ;      (high byte)",
          "006   ; 003: MVI B",
          "004   ;      4",
          "076   ; 005: MVI A",
          "000   ;      0",
          "206   ; 007: ADD M   ← loop",
          "043   ; 010: INX H",
          "005   ; 011: DCR B",
          "302   ; 012: JNZ loop",
          "007   ;      address 007 (low byte)",
          "000   ;      (high byte)",
          "323   ; 015: OUT 377",
          "377   ;      port 377",
          "166   ; 017: HLT",
          "005   ; 020: data: 5",
          "012   ; 021: data: 10",
          "024   ; 022: data: 20",
          "050   ; 023: data: 40"
        ],
        "output": [
          "LEDS ○●○○●○●● = 75"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "al9-l2-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "Which register pair points into the table?",
          "options": [
            "HL",
            "BC",
            "DE",
            "SP"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "M always means the byte at HL."
        },
        {
          "id": "al9-l2-e2",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does the example add up?",
          "options": [
            "The 4 bytes of the table",
            "The numbers 1 to 4",
            "HL",
            "Nothing"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "5 + 10 + 20 + 40 = 75."
        },
        {
          "id": "al9-l2-e3",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does INX H do in the loop?",
          "options": [
            "Moves to the next byte of the table",
            "Counts the rounds",
            "Adds to A",
            "Ends the loop"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "B counts, HL walks."
        },
        {
          "id": "al9-l2-e4",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What do the lights show?",
          "code": [
            "041   ; 000: LXI H t",
            "020   ;      address 020 (low byte)",
            "000   ;      (high byte)",
            "006   ; 003: MVI B",
            "003   ;      3",
            "076   ; 005: MVI A",
            "000   ;      0",
            "206   ; 007: ADD M   ← loop",
            "043   ; 010: INX H",
            "005   ; 011: DCR B",
            "302   ; 012: JNZ loop",
            "007   ;      address 007 (low byte)",
            "000   ;      (high byte)",
            "323   ; 015: OUT 377",
            "377   ;      port 377",
            "166   ; 017: HLT",
            "001   ; 020: data: 1",
            "002   ; 021: data: 2",
            "003   ; 022: data: 3"
          ],
          "options": [
            "6",
            "3",
            "2",
            "1"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "1 + 2 + 3."
        },
        {
          "id": "al9-l2-e5",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "Why does the table come after HLT?",
          "options": [
            "So it's never run as instructions",
            "Tables must be at the end",
            "HLT protects it",
            "No reason"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Data bytes would be read as opcodes otherwise."
        },
        {
          "id": "al9-l2-e6",
          "type": "order_lines",
          "prompt": "Put the loop body in order.",
          "lines": [
            "206   ; ADD M",
            "043   ; INX H",
            "005   ; DCR B"
          ],
          "answer": [
            "206   ; ADD M",
            "043   ; INX H",
            "005   ; DCR B"
          ],
          "explanation": "Add the byte, move on, count down. JNZ follows."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "al9-l3",
      "title": "Multiplying with a Loop",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "With a loop, multiplying is easy: add the first number as many times as the second one says.",
        "Division works backwards: subtract again and again while it fits, and count the rounds.",
        "These routines were the first things every Altair owner wrote, because the 8080 can't multiply or divide by itself."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "016   ; 000: MVI C",
          "014   ;      12",
          "006   ; 002: MVI B",
          "015   ;      13",
          "076   ; 004: MVI A",
          "000   ;      0",
          "201   ; 006: ADD C   ← loop",
          "005   ; 007: DCR B",
          "302   ; 010: JNZ loop",
          "006   ;      address 006 (low byte)",
          "000   ;      (high byte)",
          "323   ; 013: OUT 377",
          "377   ;      port 377",
          "166   ; 015: HLT"
        ],
        "output": [
          "LEDS ●○○●●●○○ = 156"
        ]
      },
